{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /Users/zhangbowen/.codex/skills/or-llm-agent/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: or-llm-agent\ndescription: Generate and verify Gurobi optimization-model submissions for OR-CI pilots through the packaged OR-LLM-Agent CLI. Use when working on OR model generation, BWOR pilots, OR-CI integration, generated Gurobi submissions, or `or_llm_agent` evaluation workflows.\n---\n\n# OR-LLM-Agent\n\nUse the `or-llm-agent` CLI as the deterministic execution surface. The skill is an operating guide only; do not reimplement the CLI workflow in ad hoc scripts unless the CLI is broken and you are fixing it.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nRun a local readiness check before OR-CI pilot generation:\n\n```bash\nuv run or-llm-agent health --agent\n```\n\nRun a BWOR pilot batch:\n\n```bash\nuv run or-llm-agent pilot \\\n  --mode agent \\\n  --ids BWOR-001 BWOR-002 BWOR-010 \\\n  --artifact-dir ../or-ci/artifacts/pilot/phase-1-integration-2026-05-16-rerun\n```\n\nFor direct API-provider generation, check provider health and use `--mode api`\nexplicitly when clarity matters:\n\n```bash\nuv run or-llm-agent health --model o3-mini --live\nuv run or-llm-agent pilot \\\n  --mode api \\\n  --ids BWOR-001 BWOR-002 BWOR-010 \\\n  --model o3-mini \\\n  --artifact-dir ../or-ci/artifacts/pilot/api-rerun\n```\n\nFor a single problem, generate then verify:\n\n```bash\nuv run or-llm-agent generate \\\n  --mode agent \\\n  --bwor-id BWOR-001 \\\n  --out submission.py \\\n  --raw raw.txt\n\nuv run or-llm-agent verify \\\n  --problem ../or-ci/tests/fixtures/bwor/BWOR-001/problem.json \\\n  --submission submission.py \\\n  --out report.json\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Prefer `health --agent` and `pilot --mode agent` for OR-CI pilot work.\n2. Use `health --live` and `--mode api` only when intentionally testing direct provider calls.\n3. Use `pilot` for BWOR batches so raw responses, submissions, reports, `summary.json`, and `report.md` stay together.\n4. Use `generate` plus `verify` for one-off inspection or debugging.\n5. Inspect `summary.json`, `report.md`, and individual OR-CI reports before answering the user.\n6. Treat OR-CI `SUCCESS` as \"configured invariants passed,\" not proof of full mathematical correctness.\n\n## Interpretation Rules\n\n- `generation_mode` distinguishes direct `api` generation from nested Codex `agent` generation.\n- `generation_status` describes provider/code extraction or agent artifact outcome.\n- `agent_returncode` is the nested `codex exec` process exit code in agent mode.\n- OR-CI `classification` describes verifier outcome after a submission exists.\n- Provider errors and subprocess logs should be redacted by the CLI; do not paste unredacted API errors into notes or answers.\n- Generated submissions must expose `def build_model(data: dict)` and return an unoptimized `gurobipy.Model`.\n- OR-CI remains standalone. Do not add OpenAI, Anthropic, or dotenv dependencies to `or-ci`.\n\n## Expected Artifacts\n\nPilot runs should write:\n\n- `raw/<BWOR-ID>.txt`\n- `submissions/<BWOR-ID>.py`\n- `reports/<BWOR-ID>.json`\n- `sessions/<BWOR-ID>/codex-events.jsonl` in agent mode\n- `sessions/<BWOR-ID>/last-message.md` in agent mode\n- `agent-status/<BWOR-ID>.json` in agent mode\n- `summary.json`\n- `report.md`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
